ed in a way that produces shippable engineering artifacts, it's broad enough to swallow resources without clear milestones, and its primary value proposition (thought leadership positioning) isn't an engineering outcome I'm accountable for.\n\nPromise score: Maybe 15-20. The idea of having reference schemas has some technical utility, but the way this is scoped — as a public benchmark across architectures with no concrete tie to our actual systems — makes it very low priority from my perspective. It's not that logging isn't important (it absolutely is), but this particular framing doesn't produce engineering velocity for us.\n",
