esearch — it's engineering plumbing that I know how to build with confidence.\n\nI'd say this is an approve with a high promise score. The technical approach is sound, well within our capabilities, fast to prototype, and directly addresses a regulatory requirement. The only mild concern is whether \"live\" updates on every commit creates noise or maintenance issues, but that's a tunable parameter in implementation.\n\nPromise: I'd give this around 82-85. It's very doable, clearly needed, and fast to prototype. Not a 100 because there are some integration complexities (ensuring the output format maps correctly to regulatory requirements, handling the \"lifetime\" aspect of documentation which may require archiving strategies), and the \"live\" aspect could become a maintenance liability if not carefully scoped. But it's clearly above my approval threshold.\n",
