y positive IF executed well, but \"gold standard\" overclaim is risky\n\nI think I'll reject this. It's a nice-sounding idea that sounds like it addresses the regulation but actually misses the point of what Article 12 requires in practice. The generic DL framework wrapper approach doesn't map to the specific operational events required by Art 12(2) and (3). And committing our scarce resources to build an open-source library for \"the global research community\" when we haven't yet ensured our own high-risk systems technically allow for automatic recording of events over their lifetime is a misallocation.\n\nPromise score: I'd say around 25-30. There's some conceptual alignment (logging, documentation), but the execution path described doesn't match what Article 12 actually requires, and the resource allocation logic is wrong from my perspective.\n",
