pproval bottleneck for my team. Before I can prototype, I need to pass through this gate. If the gate is slow or unclear, it directly impacts speed.\n- However, on the flip side: having a clear determination of whether a system IS high-risk does help me scope my technical work. Without it, I might over-engineer logging for non-high-risk systems or under-build for ones that need it. So there's a scoping value.\n\nBut overall, this is a governance/process layer that adds overhead to prototyping without providing any technical solution for the actual logging infrastructure. It doesn't make me faster or produce higher-quality prototypes. The quarterly cadence is too slow for agile development. And it's fundamentally not a technical proposal - it's an organizational one. From my vantage point (technical viability and speed/quality of prototyping), this adds friction without delivering engineering value.\n\nI'll reject this but give it a moderate-ish score because the scoping function has some indirect value to me, even though the mechanism is wrong for my needs.\n",
