nd and necessary for Annex III 1(a) systems.\n\nI'd lean toward approving this because:\n- It's narrowly scoped (specifically Article 12(3)(d))\n- It addresses a clear legal requirement that can't be avoided\n- The resource commitment is bounded (it's an interface + logging, not a research program)\n- It's a necessary component of compliance\n\nBut my promise score should reflect the concern about potential inefficiency in implementation approach. I'd say maybe 62-70 range. It's clearly needed but the \"build a new portal\" framing gives me pause from an efficiency standpoint. If it's done by extending existing systems, great. If they spin up a whole new application stack, that's wasteful.\n\nLet me settle on: approve, promise around 65. It's a necessary, well-scoped compliance item, but the implementation approach as described (building a \"specialized interface\" and \"secure authentication portal\") raises efficiency concerns about whether existing infrastructure is being leveraged optimally.\n",
