time (Article 12(2)(c)), that's a compliance gap. A dashboard could make this practical. But \"practical\" doesn't mean the dashboard itself is required — you could do post-market monitoring through other means (reporting, periodic reviews, etc.).\n\nI'll reject with a promise of around 40-50. It has some utility but isn't where I'd allocate scarce compliance resources first.\n",
