equirements.\n4. Governance around which events must be captured per system category.\n\nOverall, this is a strong proposal from a compliance standpoint. It directly addresses the core requirement of Article 12(1) and provides infrastructure to meet 12(2) and potentially 12(3). The centralized approach reduces variability in implementation quality across teams. I would approve it but note that the specific technical specifications need to be validated against the exact regulatory text before full deployment.\n\nMy promise score: This is very well-aligned with my compliance mandate. It's a foundational piece of infrastructure for meeting Article 12 requirements. The main risk is incomplete specification (hashes vs. data, missing reference DB), but those are implementation details that can be addressed in design. I'd give this a high score — around 82-85. It's not a perfect 90+ because there are specific gaps (input hashes vs. actual data recording, no explicit mention of reference database tracking, no log retention policy) that need to be resolved before it fully satisfies the regulation from my perspective.\n\nLet me settle on 83.\n",
