 need to note that Article 12(3) has very specific minimum requirements for biometric systems that a generic \"framework\" might not automatically capture without explicit configuration.\n\nOverall assessment: This is a strong, directly relevant proposal that addresses the core requirement of Article 12. It's well-scoped, architecturally sound from a compliance perspective, and addresses systemic risk. The main gap is whether it explicitly covers the Annex III 1(a) specific requirements, but as a framework it provides the foundation for that. I would approve this — it's essentially implementing the law's primary technical requirement in a way that protects the institution.\n\nPromise score: This is very close to what Article 12 demands. The main deduction is for not explicitly calling out the Annex III 1(a) specific fields and for not mentioning data retention/GDPR interaction, but those could be implementation details within the framework. I'd put this at around 82-85. It's a strong compliance enabler with minor gaps in explicit specification of all sub-requirements.\n\nLet me settle on 83.\n",
