        "reasoning_content": "The user asks me to screen proposal P2568 from the vantage point of a Compliance Officer at an R&D institution developing AI systems subject to the EU AI Act. My domain of concern is: institutional survival, regulatory compliance, and market reputation.\n\nLet me analyze the proposal:\n\n**Proposal P2568: Post-Market Risk Detection Dashboard**\n- An analytics tool monitoring system logs in real time for performance drift or high-risk anomalies\n- Flags events that could constitute a substantial modification under the law\n- Uses statistical process control to scan operational logs for patterns indicating increased risk levels\n- Alerts trigger immediate compliance reviews\n- Claims to fulfill Article 12(2) by facilitating proactive post-market monitoring and mitigating institutional liability\n\nLet me assess this from my compliance officer vantage point:\n\n**Strengths:**\n- Directly addresses Article 12(2)(b): \"facilitating the post-market monitoring referred to in Article 72\"\n- Also touches on Article 12(2)(a): identifying situations that may result in presenting a risk (Article 79(1)) or substantial modification\n- Real-time monitoring of logs aligns with the spirit of Article 12(1) which requires automatic recording, and then adds an analytical layer on top\n- The concept of flagging \"substantial modification\" is important because under the EU AI Act, a substantial modification can trigger re-assessment obligations\n- Alerting to compliance reviews creates an audit trail showing proactive compliance posture — good for market reputation and institutional survival\n- Statistical process control (SPC) is a well-established methodology in quality management; it's concrete and implementable\n\n**Weaknesses/Concerns:**\n- The proposal says \"fulfills Article 12(2)\" but Article 12 is about *record-keeping* — the logging capabilities themselves. This dashboard is an analytical layer ON TOP of logs, which is more aligned with Articles