rror.\n\nThe gaps (Annex III specific requirements, person identification, substantial modification tracking) are implementation details that would be addressed in the actual build specification rather than disqualifying the proposal at this screening stage. The core architecture is sound and directly responsive to the regulatory text.\n\nThis clearly meets my bar for approval from a compliance standpoint. It's not a vague \"we'll think about it\" - it's a concrete technical solution that maps well to the regulatory requirements. The institutional risk of NOT having this (for high-risk systems) would be severe - potential market withdrawal orders, fines, and reputational damage in the EU market.\n\nDecision: Approve.\nPromise score: This is a strong alignment with core Article 12 obligations. I'd put it around 85-90. The gaps noted above (explicit Annex III 1(a) fields, person identification, substantial modification event capture) prevent a perfect 100, but the architecture is fundamentally sound and addresses the primary regulatory requirement. I'll go with 87.\n",
