ight be sufficient.\n\nThe mandate requires automatic recording of events logs, and specific logging capabilities. Sidecar intercepts inputs/outputs. That seems effective. I'd give 4? Could be 3 because effectiveness depends on implementation details for Article 12(3). But proposal says log event metadata. Probably will solve main problem. Let's give 3 = contributes.\n\nApplicability: solves identified problem directly related to stated problem. Yes do X to get Y and Y is part of stated problem. So 4.\n\nParadigm_relatedness: degree to which idea preserves or modifies paradigm. Introduces new elements but still treats compliance as logging practice? Sidecar decouples regulatory logging from research logic to maintain prototyping speed. That's slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice. So level 2.\n\nOriginality: degree rare and ingenious. Sidecar pattern for compliance is common? Maybe unusual, interesting. Not expressed before AND ingenious? Might be 3 = unusual, interesting; shows some imagination. Or 2 = interesting. Sidecar pattern is known in microservices. Might be common mundane. Hmm. Automated compliance sidecar is somewhat known. I'd say 2 = interesting.\n\nLet's output JSON? Instructions say return rating echoing its id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence then <subscale>. Probably structured.\n\nWe'll produce:\n\nid: P1044\nimplementability_evidence: ...\nimplementability: 3\n...\n\nProvide one sentence evidence.\n\nMake sure evidence sentence first then score.\n\nProbably output as lines.\n\nLet's produce clean format.\n\n",
